<title>USA: N.Y. business loans rose $699 mln in Feb 5 week.</title>
<headline>N.Y. business loans rose $699 mln in Feb 5 week.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-02-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Commercial and industrial loans at the six major New York banks, excluding acceptances, rose $699 million to $43,965 million in the week ended February 5, the Federal Reserve Bank of New York said.</p>
<p>Including acceptances, loans rose $700 million to $44,198 million.</p>
<p>Commercial paper outstanding nationally rose $4,591 million to $821,721 million.</p>
<p>-- N.A. Treasury Desk, 212-859-1660</p>
</text>
